er-election-role (Role) | mlflow-operator-controller-manager |\n229\t| leader-election-rolebinding | system | leader-election-role (Role) | controller-manager |\n230\t| manager-rolebinding | system | manager-role (Role) | controller-manager |\n231\t\n232\t### Secrets\n233\t\n234\t| Secret Name | Type | Purpose | Provisioned By | Auto-Rotate |\n235\t|-----------|----|-------|--------------|-----------|\n236\t\n237\t### Authentication & Authorization\n238\t\n239\t| Endpoint | Methods | Auth Mechanism | Enforcement Point | Policy |\n240\t|--------|-------|--------------|-----------------|------|\n241\t| :8081/healthz | GET | None | N/A | Kubernetes health probe; unauthenticated by design |\n242\t| :8081/readyz | GET | None | N/A | Kubernetes readiness probe; unauthenticated by design |\n243\t| Named Secret access (mlflow-artifact-connection) | Kubernetes API | RBAC with resourceNames restriction | kube-apiserver | mlflow-operator-manager-role restricts secret access to mlflow-artifact-connection only |\n244\t| Named Secret access (mlflow-artifact-connection) | Kubernetes API | RBAC with resourceNames restriction | kube-apiserver | manager-role restricts secret access to mlflow-artifact-connection only |\n245\t| Kubernetes API | REST | ServiceAccount token (in-cluster) | kube-apiserver | RBAC enforced via mlflow-operator-manager-role ClusterRole; SA mlflow-operator-controller-manager |\n246\t| :8443/metrics | GET | TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview (controller-runtime authn/authz filter) | controller-runtime metrics authn/authz filter | RBAC via mlflow-operator-metrics-auth-role; exposed by Service mlflow-operator-controller-manager-metrics-service; controller-runtime generated self-signed TLS certificate |\n247\t\n248\t### Security Evidence\n249\t\n250\t| Kind | Target | Detail | Signal Type |\n251\t|----|------|------|-----------|\n252\t| tls-config | crypto/tls | TLS configuration import | dependency-signal |\n253\t\n254\t### FIPS Compliance\n255\t\n256\t#### Build-Time FIPS (check-payload gate)\n257\t\n258\t| Aspect | Value | Source |\n259\t|--------|-------|--------|\n260\t| **Build flags** | GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime, -tags strictfipsruntime | Dockerfile.konflux:32 |\n261\t| **Linking** | Dynamic (CGO_ENABLED=1) | Dockerfile.konflux:31 |\n262\t| **OpenSSL in image** | Yes (via UBI9 go-toolset builder and ubi9-minimal runtime base) | Dockerfile.konflux:2, Dockerfile.konflux:34 |\n263\t| **OLM FIPS annotation** | not extracted | -- |\n264\t\n265\t#### Application-Level Crypto\n266\t\n267\t| Aspect | Value | Source |\n268\t|--------|-------|--------|\n269\t| **TLS configuration** | Uses crypto/tls via controller-runtime metrics server; supports operator-provided or auto-generated self-signed certificates | cmd/main.go:261-284 |\n270\t| **Crypto libraries** | stdlib crypto/tls (FIPS via OpenSSL with strictfipsruntime) | cmd/main.go, go.mod |\n271\t| **Certificate handling** | Configurable cert path via flags; falls back to controller-runtime self-signed certs | cmd/main.go:278-284 |\n272\t| **Non-FIPS crypto risks** | None detected; strictfipsruntime enforces FIPS-approved algorithms at runtime | Dockerfile.konflux:32 |\n273\t## Data Flows\n274\t\n275\t- **Control plane reconciliation:** The operator watches MLflow, MLflowOperator, and MLflowConfig CRs, ConfigMaps, and owned resources (Deployments, Services, Jobs, PVCs, Secrets, ServiceAccounts). On reconciliation, the MLflowReconciler renders Helm charts into Kubernetes objects and applies them via the Kubernetes API (port 6443, TLS, ServiceAccount token auth). Owned resources are label-filtered (`app=mlflow`) to minimize watch bandwidth. [source: cmd/main.go:293-318, internal/controller/mlflow_controller.go:473-552]\n276\t- **Conditional platform integration:** At startup, the operator probes the Kubernetes discovery API for Gateway API, ConsoleLink, ServiceMonitor, and MLflowOperator CRDs. When present, additional watches and owned-resource management are activated; when absent, the operator operates without those integrations. [source: internal/controller/routing.go:46-179, internal/controller/mlflow_controller.go:528-552]\n277\t- **Workspace RBAC propagation:** The NamespaceRBACReconciler watches the platform Auth CR (`services.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1`), MLflow CRs, and labeled namespaces. When a namespace carries the `opendatahub.io/mlflow-workspace` label, the controller creates RoleBindings referencing the mlflow-view and mlflow-edit ClusterRoles, enabling workspace-scoped multi-tenant access. [source: internal/controller/namespace_rbac_controller.go:48-106, 135-154]\n278\t- **Metrics and observability:** The operator exposes a TLS-protected metrics endpoint on port 8443 with TokenReview/SubjectAccessReview enforcement, accessible only to subjects authorized by the `mlflow-operator-metrics-auth-role` ClusterRole. A ClusterIP Service fronts this endpoint. Health and readiness probes on port 8081 are unauthenticated. [source: cmd/main.go:261-284, config/base/metrics_service.yaml:1]\n279\t\n280\t## Integration Points\n281\t\n282\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Watches); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: MLflowOperatorReconciler. [source: config/base/metrics_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/namespace_role.yaml:11, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, go.mod]\n283\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Watches); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: MLflowReconciler. [source: config/base/metrics_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/namespace_role.yaml:11, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, go.mod]\n284\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Resource read; purpose: get operations by MLflowOperatorReconciler, MLflowReconciler. [source: config/base/metrics_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/namespace_role.yaml:11, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, go.mod]\n285\t- **/v1/Namespace:** Controller watch (For); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: NamespaceRBACReconciler. [source: config/base/metrics_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/namespace_role.yaml:11, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, go.mod]\n286\t- **