{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-01c4796e-efa5-46cc-8916-aad0b23f00ac","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8048e4ff794b5dc5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-6bd4guuy/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E001.md","content":"# Validate workspace-resolution initialization dependencies for artifacts-only serving\n\n## Description\n\nInvestigation resolving whether workspace resolution in `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` (and the `kubernetes://` workspace store it reads) can initialize and answer experiment-to-workspace lookups in an MLflow server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized. The strategy flags this as an open question and as an assumption needing validation; the answer determines whether the plugin requires refactoring before a workspace-aware artifacts-only server mode can be built, and shapes the server's initialization sequence for that mode. It also validates the related assumption that artifact request paths carry enough information to resolve workspace membership.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Trace the initialization path of the Kubernetes auth plugin's workspace resolution (registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) and of the `kubernetes://` workspace store.\n- Identify every dependency of that initialization path on tracking store or model registry store initialization.\n- Determine whether the workspace store's experiment-to-workspace mapping is answerable without initializing tracking stores.\n- Determine whether artifact request paths under the S3 artifact store structure (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`) carry sufficient information (experiment ID or run ID) to resolve workspace membership.\n- If coupling is found: produce a refactor plan that factors workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, listing the interfaces the server and the plugin will use — sufficient to scope the follow-on implementation without re-analysis.\n- Deliverable: written findings with code-level evidence plus a reproducible minimal harness or automated test demonstrating resolution behavior with tracking stores uninitialized.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The findings document states, with code-level evidence (file and function call paths), whether workspace-resolution initialization depends on tracking or model registry store initialization, and whether experiment-to-workspace mapping is accessible without tracking stores.\n- A reproducible minimal harness (or automated test) demonstrates workspace resolution succeeding or failing in a context with no tracking store initialized — the outcome is observable, not asserted.\n- If coupling is found, the refactor plan specifies the independent initialization path, the interfaces involved, and the changes needed in the plugin and any server-side hooks.\n- If artifact request paths are insufficient to resolve workspace membership for the S3 artifact store path structure, the findings state so explicitly and identify what additional context the request path would need to carry.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-7 (P1)** — resolves the unknown gating auth plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context (strategy open question: \"Does the workspace store initialization in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins depend on tracking store availability?\").\n- Validates the assumptions underpinning **HLR-1 (P0)** and **HLR-2 (P0)**: workspace store accessible without tracking stores; artifact paths resolvable to workspace membership.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":73815,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b018caeaf481d689","agent_id":"aace295bef333efa4","session_id":"3b7a323d-7ff9-406d-be9e-97ebfbbc4b7a","uuid":"a36934f8-4eab