{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-532fffed-0cea-490f-a6b7-3f50e98790ee","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-82de852200a82c8b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-6bd4guuy/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E003.md","content":"# Plugin workspace resolution for the artifacts-only server context\n\n## Description\n\nMake the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin's workspace resolution function correctly in an artifacts-only MLflow server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized. Where the initialization-dependency investigation finds that resolution is coupled to the full tracking server initialization path, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin so the artifacts-only server can use it. The plugin continues to provide experiment-to-workspace mapping through the existing plugin infrastructure; the authentication setup (kube-rbac-proxy sidecar, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) is unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify and extend the plugin's experiment-to-workspace resolution so it can be invoked from artifact request handling with only the workspace store (`kubernetes://`) available — no tracking store or model registry store initialization.\n- If the investigation found coupling to the tracking server's full initialization path: refactor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, preserving existing tracking-server behavior (per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n- Support resolution from artifact requests whose parent experiment is identifiable under the S3 artifact store path structure (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`); document limitations for non-standard artifact roots.\n- Reuse the existing auth plugin infrastructure — the strategy deliberately does not dictate Kubernetes API mechanics inside the plugin (Staff Engineer input); implementation-level choices remain with the team.\n- Automated tests covering resolution in the no-tracking-store context, plus regression tests for the existing tracking-server resolution path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workspace resolution returns the correct workspace assignment for an experiment via the `kubernetes://` workspace store in a server context with no tracking or model registry store initialized, demonstrated by automated tests.\n- Resolution is invocable given an artifact request path's parent experiment identifier (S3 artifact store path structure).\n- If refactored: the independent initialization path is exercised by tests that initialize workspace resolution without any tracking store, and the refactor plan's interfaces are implemented as specified.\n- Existing tracking-server workspace resolution behavior is unchanged (regression tests pass) and the authentication setup is untouched.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-7 (P1)** — auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization.\n- Priority note: P0 by inheritance — this capability enables the P0 workspace-aware artifacts-only server mode (HLR-1 through HLR-4).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":75257,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b018caeaf481d689","agent_id":"aace295bef333efa4","session_id":"3b7a323d-7ff9-406d-be9e-97ebfbbc4b7a","uuid":"56aa5e34-9707-4ee1-8636-868d53c94f2c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:51:00.865Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
