{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-40de4f3c-2ccf-4ae8-b943-132a0bd4b6d9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-930c14804880c3db","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-6bd4guuy/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E005.md","content":"# MLflow operator split-server topology for dedicated artifacts-only serving\n\n## Description\n\nExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, and configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated instance — a split-server topology, not a single-deployment configuration toggle (Staff Engineer input). The main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry; the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. Users configure a single MLflow CR; the operator manages the split topology declaratively.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New Helm chart templates within the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (MLflow CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply) for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute.\n- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms already used for the main tracking deployment.\n- Configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated instance per the routing approach determined by the artifact traffic routing investigation (Gateway API HTTPRoute-level routing, or tracking-server delegation if that outcome is selected).\n- Create HTTPRoute resources conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n- Deploy the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment.\n- Operator validation that rejects MLflow CR configurations enabling the split topology where the artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags — misconfiguration must not silently bypass workspace validation (strategy risk mitigation).\n- Validate early that the chart architecture supports a second Deployment without structural changes (strategy assumption); if structural changes turn out to be required, re-plan within this epic before proceeding.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Reconciling an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct rendered Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command includes `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the rendered Deployment spec.\n- The main tracking deployment's configuration routes artifact traffic to the dedicated instance per the selected routing approach.\n- HTTPRoute creation follows the operator's conditional CRD discovery pattern (no hard dependency on Gateway API resources when the CRDs are absent).\n- The operator rejects MLflow CR configurations that enable the split topology without workspace flags on the artifacts-only instance.\n- The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar is deployed on the artifacts-only Deployment, matching the main tracking deployment's authentication setup.\n- End-to-end verification against a server image supporting workspace-aware artifacts-only serving: artifact requests through the dedicated instance return HTTP 200 for workspace members and HTTP 403 for non-members. (This acceptance criterion gates the first end-to-end execution; the operator work itself proceeds in parallel with the server-side capability — the flag combination it renders is a configuration reference, not a build-against artifact.)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-5 (P1)** — operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n- **HLR-6 (P1)** — main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":77032,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b018caeaf481d689","agent_id":"aace295bef333efa4","session_id":"3b7a323d-7ff9-406d-be9e-97ebfbbc4b7a","uuid":"a5ba6fe8-3e3c-4e9b-85d1-676a0a26426e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:51:22.517Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
