{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0acbfb75d1a07a3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: Plugin workspace resolution for the artifacts-only server context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: add_remediation\n14\t  fallback_approach: If workspace resolution is coupled to tracking store initialization,\n15\t    add the refactor work that factors resolution into an independent initialization\n16\t    path within the plugin (path prescribed by the strategy's risk mitigation); if\n17\t    not coupled, verification only.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Plugin workspace resolution for the artifacts-only server context\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tMake the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin's workspace resolution function correctly in an artifacts-only MLflow server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized. Where the initialization-dependency investigation finds that resolution is coupled to the full tracking server initialization path, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin so the artifacts-only server can use it. The plugin continues to provide experiment-to-workspace mapping through the existing plugin infrastructure; the authentication setup (kube-rbac-proxy sidecar, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) is unchanged.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Verify and extend the plugin's experiment-to-workspace resolution so it can be invoked from artifact request handling with only the workspace store (`kubernetes://`) available — no tracking store or model registry store initialization.\n44\t- If the investigation found coupling to the tracking server's full initialization path: refactor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, preserving existing tracking-server behavior (per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n45\t- Support resolution from artifact requests whose parent experiment is identifiable under the S3 artifact store path structure (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`); document limitations for non-standard artifact roots.\n46\t- Reuse the existing auth plugin infrastructure — the strategy deliberately does not dictate Kubernetes API mechanics inside the plugin (Staff Engineer input); implementation-level choices remain with the team.\n47\t- Automated tests covering resolution in the no-tracking-store context, plus regression tests for the existing tracking-server resolution path.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Workspace resolution returns the correct workspace assignment for an experiment via the `kubernetes://` workspace store in a server context with no tracking or model registry store initialized, demonstrated by automated tests.\n52\t- Resolution is invocable given an artifact request path's parent experiment identifier (S3 artifact store path structure).\n53\t- If refactored: the independent initialization path is exercised by tests that initialize workspace resolution without any tracking store, and the refactor plan's interfaces are implemented as specified.\n54\t- Existing tracking-server workspace resolution behavior is unchanged (regression tests pass) and the authentication setup is untouched.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- **HLR-7 (P1)** — auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization.\n59\t- Priority note: P0 by inheritance — this capability enables the P0 workspace-aware artifacts-only server mode (HLR-1 through HLR-4).\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab83309557091ef2","agent_id":"ad761b13213c7f400","session_id":"3b7a323d-7ff9-406d-be9e-97ebfbbc4b7a","uuid":"24b90f53-962a-4c49-8331-8ee42384168d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:54:00.976Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0acbfb75d1a07a3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
