{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4323e5d3e13c292","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator split-server topology for dedicated artifacts-only serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing determination selects server-side delegation instead\n15\t    of HTTPRoute-level routing, the main-deployment routing configuration and HTTPRoute\n16\t    design are rewritten to the selected approach, and the conditional tracking-server\n17\t    delegation epic in branch B applies.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# MLflow operator split-server topology for dedicated artifacts-only serving\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, and configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated instance — a split-server topology, not a single-deployment configuration toggle (Staff Engineer input). The main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry; the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. Users configure a single MLflow CR; the operator manages the split topology declaratively.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- New Helm chart templates within the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (MLflow CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply) for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute.\n44\t- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms already used for the main tracking deployment.\n45\t- Configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated instance per the routing approach determined by the artifact traffic routing investigation (Gateway API HTTPRoute-level routing, or tracking-server delegation if that outcome is selected).\n46\t- Create HTTPRoute resources conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n47\t- Deploy the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment.\n48\t- Operator validation that rejects MLflow CR configurations enabling the split topology where the artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags — misconfiguration must not silently bypass workspace validation (strategy risk mitigation).\n49\t- Validate early that the chart architecture supports a second Deployment without structural changes (strategy assumption); if structural changes turn out to be required, re-plan within this epic before proceeding.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Reconciling an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct rendered Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n54\t- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command includes `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the rendered Deployment spec.\n55\t- The main tracking deployment's configuration routes artifact traffic to the dedicated instance per the selected routing approach.\n56\t- HTTPRoute creation follows the operator's conditional CRD discovery pattern (no hard dependency on Gateway API resources when the CRDs are absent).\n57\t- The operator rejects MLflow CR configurations that enable the split topology without workspace flags on the artifacts-only instance.\n58\t- The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar is deployed on the artifacts-only Deployment, matching the main tracking deployment's authentication setup.\n59\t- End-to-end verification against a server image supporting workspace-aware artifacts-only serving: artifact requests through the dedicated instance return HTTP 200 for workspace members and HTTP 403 for non-members. (This acceptance criterion gates the first end-to-end execution; the operator work itself proceeds in parallel with the server-side capability — the flag combination it renders is a configuration reference, not a build-against artifact.)\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- **HLR-5 (P1)** — operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n64\t- **HLR-6 (P1)** — main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab83309557091ef2","agent_id":"ad761b13213c7f400","session_id":"3b7a323d-7ff9-406d-be9e-97ebfbbc4b7a","uuid":"62321801-f338-4bc6-8cf5-afce096dd82c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:54:04.281Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4323e5d3e13c292","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
