{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b961dfb6057656d2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E006\n3\ttitle: Tracking-server artifact traffic delegation to the dedicated artifacts-only\n4\t  instance\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tbranch: B\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If HTTPRoute-level routing suffices (outcome A), this epic is\n17\t    removed; artifact traffic routing is configured entirely by the operator split-server\n18\t    topology work.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Tracking-server artifact traffic delegation to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConditional epic (branch B of the artifact traffic routing determination): implemented only if the routing investigation concludes that Gateway API HTTPRoute-level routing alone cannot route artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, and the tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. In that outcome, this epic delivers the tracking-server side of the split-server topology's artifact traffic routing.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Implement the tracking-server configuration change that delegates artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, using the mechanism identified by the routing determination.\n44\t- Keep the single MLflow CR as the configuration surface: the delegation configuration is rendered and managed by the operator's existing configuration mechanisms, not managed as individual resources by users.\n45\t- Ensure delegated artifact traffic retains workspace validation at the dedicated instance and the unchanged authentication setup (kube-rbac-proxy sidecar, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`).\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- The tracking server, configured with the delegation mechanism, routes artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n50\t- Artifact requests delegated from the main tracking server are workspace-validated at the dedicated instance: HTTP 200 for workspace members, HTTP 403 for non-members.\n51\t- No existing CLI arguments, API contracts, or configuration keys change meaning for deployments that do not use the split topology.\n52\t- The delegation configuration is rendered and managed through the operator's existing configuration mechanisms, preserving the single-CR configuration surface.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- **HLR-6 (P1)** — conditional share of the requirement that the main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, applicable only when the routing determination selects server-side delegation.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab83309557091ef2","agent_id":"ad761b13213c7f400","session_id":"3b7a323d-7ff9-406d-be9e-97ebfbbc4b7a","uuid":"72af085e-0d4a-4a79-857b-ebc78f8fe7fd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:54:05.050Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b961dfb6057656d2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
